{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And the blood shall be to you for a sign.</b> To you for a sign, and not to others for a sign (there). From this that they did not apply the blood except from inside." "<b>And I will see the blood.</b> All is revealed before Him, but the Holy One, blessed be He, said: I am giving My eyes to see that you are occupied in My commandments, and I am skipping over you (there)." "<b>And I will pass over.</b> And I will have compassion. Similar to it, ״פָּסֹחַ וְהִמְלִיט״ (Isaiah 31). And I say: every פְּסִיחָה is a term of leaping and skipping. <b>And I will pass over</b> — He would leap from the houses of Israel to the houses of Egyptians, for they were dwelling this one among that one. And so, ״פּוֹסְחִים עַל שְׁתֵּי הַסְּעִפִּים״ (1 Kings 18), and so all the פִּסְחִים — they walk as if hopping. And so ״פָּסֹחַ וְהִמְלִיט״ — leaping and rescuing from among the stricken." "<b>And there shall be no plague among you.</b> But it would be upon the Egyptians. If there was an Egyptian in the house of an Israelite — could he be saved? Scripture says, ״וְלֹא יִהְיֶה בָכֶם נֶגֶף״ — but it would be upon the Egyptians who are in your houses. If there was an Israelite in the house of an Egyptian — I would say he is stricken like him? Scripture says, ״וְלֹא יִהְיֶה בָכֶם נֶגֶף״ (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:39.269292680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}